now the new president of guinea-bissau  there he is  Umar Oh Sissoko am Baloo has promised to  improve the situation for the people in  the country a place which is marked by  extreme poverty and corruption so what  is life like for ordinary people in the  West African nation well DW spoke to a  19 year old teenager Zito Urbino he is  trying to make ends meet by working on a  tourist boat he told us about his hopes  for the future and also what in his  opinion definitely has to change for  things to get better in one of the  world's poorest nations for the tourists  on these speedboats the islands of  Guinea Bissau in West Africa offer a  taste of paradise for residents like 19  year-old z2 el vino they provide the  income that allows him and his family to  survive I'm a sailors assistant which  means I take people in the boat to  Bissau and bring them back or I take  them to other islands they wish to visit  I help carry things to the boat  I also check the weather it's a big  responsibility with the clients to see  if it's worth taking the risk to sail or  not  but z2 faces many challenges in his life  he's supporting at least six other  relatives with this job I was born into  a very poor family my father does not  have work and neither does my mother  with five siblings and right now I'm the  head of the family he uses the money he  earns here to pay his education and also  that of his siblings but he says going  to school is not something you can take  for granted in a country as poor and as  dysfunctional as Guinea Bissau karaoke  I wish things would be better and that  we would have more home because in our  politics things don't go well at all for  instance we start classes and all of a  sudden it's strike strike strike and  then we lose the school year and then  the next year the same thing happens but  he's determined to forge ahead with his  plans to make a better life for himself  and his family although he says it would  be easier if politicians radically  changed their behavior their skins and  their losses they should start thinking  about others and not just themselves  they should start working for all  Ghanaians when it comes to the direction  the country should be going cito has a  clear message for the president  he he must improve the schools and offer  children new schools different than the  ones we have now to give the children a  motivation for the future Zito says his  dream is to finish his studies and to  get a job in tourism and then one day be  his own boss
 

